<v SPEAKER_5>Yeah. Yeah, I'd agree with that. From my perspective, I've said this before, number one is a purely selfish endeavor for my own personal need to express myself creatively. And I've always had that sort of relationship with YouTube for me. I am a creator, I like world building, I love the aesthetic of filmmaking and editing and all of the things that go into that. Now, if I can do that about something I'm really passionate about and something I'm really curious about, then everything that comes from that is like a symptom of it, like or an offshoot. So if you get inspired from the content, that's not what I set out for, I'm glad it happened to you. If you find a deeper personal truth, I'm glad that happened. It's not my fault. I did this for me, but you got that for you and I'm happy for you. And so I've always treated it very selfishly in this sort of personal artistic expression, followed by genuine curiosity. And then whatever comes from that, if it helps move the needle, then so be it. I don't really care. I think that I just do what I like doing and trust that if I do that properly, people will like it and it'll be a net positive at the end of the day. So I really don't think about anything else further down that line.

